    "status": "NOT_IMPLEMENTED_EXACT_COMMIT_ORDER_CONFLICT",
    "scope": "Read-only diagnosis. No product/schema/test changes and no new model or service calls.",
    "counterexample": [
      "The original markVisible mutation succeeds and commits its conservative outputVisible flag.",
      "The Action receives that acknowledgment, then its delivery signal aborts before Gateway emits the first delta, or the official SDK observes abort before its first onChunk.",
      "Original state.visible asserts delivery after await and Gateway checks canDeliver before enqueue; AI SDK also checks abort after reader.read before transforms/onChunk. Therefore recordOutput is never invoked and runtimeAgentOutput remains unchanged.",
      "A fused pre-emit native parent has already committed both visibility and first output before this acknowledgment. The same abort leaves an extra durable runtimeAgentOutput row and advanced nextOutputSequence. A child savepoint can only roll back a failure inside that parent transaction, not an abort/transform/consumer failure after it committed."
    ],
    "exactSources": [
      "convex-dev/runtimeGateway.ts760-765 (post-await delivery check)",
      "convex-dev/runtimeGateway.ts893-895 (visibility acknowledgment and delivery check)",
      "convex-dev/runtimeGateway.ts1025-1031 (await visible, canDeliver, then emit)",
      "node_modules/ai/src/generate-text/stream-text.ts1886-1905 (abort after read, before forwarding)",
      "node_modules/ai/src/generate-text/stream-text.ts1929-1942 (transforms precede onChunk eventProcessor)",
      "node_modules/ai/src/generate-text/stream-text.ts1481-1508 (official callback)",
      "node_modules/@convex-dev/agent/src/vercel/client/streaming.ts178-198 (fixed smoothStream transform)",
      "convex-dev/runtimeAgent.ts1136-1166 (first onChunk flush invokes recordOutput)"
    ],
    "deadlock": "Keeping native first output provisional until real onChunk cannot satisfy pre-ACK emission prohibition: onChunk is reached only after Gateway emits that text. Waiting for onChunk before acknowledging visibility blocks the emit needed to enter onChunk. Sending it through the official pipeline before the acknowledgment violates the requested pre-ACK callback/component prohibition.",
    "receiptLimit": "An exact durable payload/producer/operation/native attempt receipt can prevent duplicate append or suppress a matching split/coalesced callback. It cannot make already-committed output conditional on a future SDK callback or undo a post-ACK abort. A receipt mismatch can refuse later delivery, but the extra durable output/effect has already occurred. Catching an output child refusal preserves conservative visibility for that one failure phase only.",
    "requiredSemanticChange": "To proceed, the product would have to accept first output being durably published at the earlier pre-emit linearization point, including when a later SDK abort/transform/consumer failure prevents onChunk; or allow an official pipeline staging callback before the publication acknowledgment. Neither follows from the exact original failure/effect requirement and emit-nothing-before-ACK constraint. No unsafe bypass is implemented.",
    "negativeOracle": "At a fixed registered-handler fixture state, arrange an AbortController abort immediately after visibility RPC resolution and before Gateway emit. Compare original and proposed handler plus official stream pipeline: exact runtimeAgentOutput rows, nextOutputSequence, native message/stream state, visibility, first error, ledger capture/attachment, and paid call count. Original has conservative visibility with zero first-output append. A pre-emit append cannot match. Add abort after transformed read but before first onChunk, transform/consumer refusal, output-child refusal, lost ACK, wrong lease/source/attempt, tool-first and split/coalesced matching. Preserve terminal UNKNOWN/capture and independent attachment; never pay again."
  },
