    "mainFinding": "runtimeAgent.ts961-1005 already runs the original admitHandler, bindNativeOperationHandler, fresh executionContext and checkpointHandler inside one admitPreparedModelOperationV8 native transaction. There is no second Action checkpoint RPC to remove. Eight joined main calls have exactly one Action admission/checkpoint span each.",
    "mainPreparationBoundary": "Earlier prepareDirectTurnV8/saveAndPrepareContextV8 returns the selected context, operation and tentative resolutions. The Action then builds the governed model and invokes official Agent.streamText; startGeneration creates a pending native message, and DeltaStreamer creates the stream. Actual joined messages:addMessages and streams:create rows occur before every final main admission. Actual SDK-normalized params pass languageParams and nativeIdentity comparison only at the middleware. Moving reservation/permit into the earlier preparation crosses real component I/O and loses the current final post-I/O source/lease/cancellation/body fence. The permit must remain after those writes and actual request normalization.",
    "providerResolution": "Both prepared native resolutions are tentative and consumed in order. createGovernedGatewayModel validates the qualification proof and constructs the official provider synchronously; it does not acquire a service token or call the model. The installed ai-sdk-provider index.ts42-48 performs getServiceToken and fetch only inside gatewayFetch, reached by doStream/doEmbed after the final permit. Provider acquisition therefore does not itself require a separate preparation commit, but the main Agent component I/O and actual body validation do.",
    "queryFinding": "runtimeAgentQueryEmbedding.ts98-120 already composes admission and checkpoint in one admitV8 Action RPC. Its ctx.runMutation(checkpointRecall) is a same-transaction child/savepoint, not a separately committed Action RPC. It preserves admission reservations when exact reserved-body validation or the checkpoint refuses; the child rollback also contains injected partial writes. Existing query-embedding-composition.test.ts130-142,250-265 exercises that consequential behavior. Official Convex registration.ts149-155 documents the savepoint plus argument/return/context overhead. The saved scalar capture provides no separate child timing; 305 ms cannot be assigned to that child.",
    "queryPreparationBoundary": "The actual CLI contextInputsAndEmbeddingV8 native query performs direct-candidate checks first, then original ordered query preparation only on semantic fallback. After its return, the Action constructs repository/selection closures, hashes the request ID, validates the exact proposal, consumes both resolutions, constructs the official provider, checks profile/model identity, and runs embedding transformParams (field, abort signal, one-value, Unicode, byte bound, normalized text, profile/batch/request validation) before fresh admitV8. No external/provider I/O is observed between those prepared proposals and admission; replay refresh remains its own native query.",
    "conditionalQueryOption": "A future semantic-only context-input mutation could derive the exact normalized embedding request with the same pure middleware normalizer, validate all current original local pre-admission checks, then invoke the original admission plus checkpoint savepoint and return one exact-use permit. This would require moving those local validators ahead of reservation, pinning every actual value/profile/batch/snapshot/binding byte, preserving fresh Action cancellation/deadline checks, replay/uncertain behavior, and proving no intervening Action I/O. It removes a semantic-only Action admission boundary at most; it cannot cover the six measured browser cases, which do not dispatch query embedding. No implementation or timing saving is claimed. Simply treating the prepared proposal as a permit is unsafe.",
    "decision": "No remaining main dispatch pair exists. Do not remove query checkpoint savepoints, cache attempts, move a permit across official component I/O, or use a preparation proposal as authority. Keep this seam unchanged under the bounded shared-latency repair scope."
